      "id": 1,
      "text": "Girard was founded in 1868, named after Girard, Pennsylvania, the former home of trustee Charles Strong.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        3,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Girard%2C_Kansas",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first post office opened in September 1868, and the first celebration on July 4 that same year marked Independence Day.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Girard%2C_Kansas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Girard grew around the Kansas City, Fort Scott and Gulf Railroad line, hoping to outpace its rival town Crawfordsville.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Girard%2C_Kansas",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The city’s first brick building, erected in 1872, was a two‑story structure that housed Franklin Playter’s bank.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Girard%2C_Kansas",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Girard’s downtown hosts the historic First Presbyterian Church, listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Girard%2C_Kansas",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Former NFL wide‑receiver Ron Kramer, who played for the Green Bay Packers, grew up in Girard.",
